
# Project 10 - Secure Container Secrets and Credential Management

Secure Campus Records Infrastructure

## Project Overview

This project explores secure credential management and sensitive configuration protection using Docker Compose, PostgreSQL and file-based Docker secrets.

The project focuses on separating sensitive credentials from infrastructure configuration, restricting database network access, implementing persistent storage and reducing accidental credential exposure.

## Technical Objectives

- Deploy a secure PostgreSQL infrastructure environment.
- Separate credentials from Docker Compose configuration.
- Implement file-based Docker Compose secrets.
- Configure PostgreSQL password file integration.
- Restrict direct database exposure.
- Implement an internal database network.
- Configure persistent database storage.
- Implement database health monitoring.
- Prevent accidental credential publication.
- Document credential lifecycle management.

