## Credential Lifecycle Management

Credential management includes:

- Secure credential creation
- Restricted local file access
- Service-specific secret assignment
- Repository exclusion
- Credential rotation
- Secure backup management
- Credential exposure remediation

Changing the secret file alone does not automatically change an existing PostgreSQL account password.

Credential rotation requires an authorised database password update and coordinated replacement of the associated secret.

## Security Controls

| Control | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Docker Compose secrets | Separate credentials from configuration |
| POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE | Initialise PostgreSQL using a password file |
| Service-specific secret access | Restrict unnecessary credential distribution |
| Internal database network | Restrict external network connectivity |
| Database port isolation | Reduce direct database exposure |
| Git ignore configuration | Prevent accidental credential publication |
| Named Docker volume | Maintain persistent database storage |
| Health checks | Monitor database readiness |
| Non-root web execution | Reduce web service privileges |
| Read-only web filesystem | Restrict filesystem modification |

